# Shroffin brand font

**Family:** Google Sans Flex  
**Source of truth (brand kit):** `/home/yash/etc/creatives/brand/Font/`  
**Website files:** `fonts/GoogleSansFlex/`

## Always

1. Use **Google Sans Flex** for every piece of text on the Shroffin website — nav, headlines, body, buttons, flyouts, future pages.
2. Load fonts via local `@font-face` from `fonts/GoogleSansFlex/` — not Google Fonts CDN, Montserrat, Inter, Roboto, Arial-as-primary, or system UI stacks as the main face.
3. CSS stack: `'Google Sans Flex', Arial, sans-serif` (or `var(--font-brand)` when defined).
4. If adding weights, copy matching `GoogleSansFlex_72pt-*.ttf` files from the brand kit Font folder into `fonts/GoogleSansFlex/`.
5. Use only the font’s natural spacing. Pick a **weight** (and size) when needed — do not invent letter-spacing, tracking, or other type “polish” rules.

## Weight map

| CSS weight | File |
|---|---|
| 100 | GoogleSansFlex_72pt-Thin.ttf |
| 200 | GoogleSansFlex_72pt-ExtraLight.ttf |
| 300 | GoogleSansFlex_72pt-Light.ttf |
| 400 | GoogleSansFlex_72pt-Regular.ttf |
| 500 | GoogleSansFlex_72pt-Medium.ttf |
| 600 | GoogleSansFlex_72pt-SemiBold.ttf |
| 700 | GoogleSansFlex_72pt-Bold.ttf |
| 800 | GoogleSansFlex_72pt-ExtraBold.ttf |
| 900 | GoogleSansFlex_72pt-Black.ttf |

## Never

- Do not use Montserrat (legacy site) on the redesigned home page.
- Do not invent a different brand typeface without an explicit user request.
- Do not add `letter-spacing`, tracking, or calm product-site kerning tweaks. Let Google Sans Flex render as designed.
